# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# D-93 with A3, the two-formal helper under --walk-methods: the walked host's call of a nested method is a CALL of
# any number of inputs -- two actuals and the capture n -- so the host is walked (it stayed native, noted, while
# the call went through l2_mad_call's one input).  add(1) = 9.  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: h2 (int: y; int: z) int
        return: n + y + z
    int: q (h2: 1 2)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: q + x
    return: addN

@: add makeAdder(5)
int: a (add: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 9
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
